node_modules/

# Explicitly un-ignore, because the SUPER-REPO root .gitignore carries a blanket
# `dist/`. Without this negation the directory is excluded before git descends
# into it, and every future build would need `git add -f` — a delivery channel
# that depends on someone remembering a flag is not a delivery channel.
!dist/
!dist/**

# dist/ is TRACKED, deliberately. It is not "a build artifact in git" by
# accident — it is this vessel's DELIVERY CHANNEL.
#
# The substrate updates itself by pulling this repo. The surface's systemd unit
# runs src/index.ts, which serves ui/dist; nothing rebuilds on pull, and
# post_install builds exactly once at install time. So while dist/ was ignored
# there was NO path by which a UI source change reached a deployed surface — a
# container could sit on current source and serve a bundle built the night
# before, which is exactly what both deployments were doing (observed
# 2026-08-08: source at 85122e84, bundle from 20:42 the previous evening).
#
# Tracking it means a pull delivers a working surface with no toolchain, no
# build step at boot that can fail, and no private-clone credential needed just
# to render a page. Vite content-hashes filenames and empties the directory each
# build, so this replaces rather than accumulates.
#
# THE COST, stated plainly: a ui/src change is only live once its rebuilt dist
# is committed WITH it. scripts/git-hooks/pre-commit enforces that for commits
# that run hooks. A commit path that bypasses hooks does not get the check.

# Scratch HOME for container builds. The build runs as the host user inside
# `oven/bun:1` so nothing lands root-owned in the tree; bun wants a writable
# HOME for its cache, and that cache is not a file git should carry.
.container-home/
